47375f2ccecb6b20d0de962e565e\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review: I read packet.json in full (the entire frozen task material) and the declared Audit A, self-containment, and NL0-format rules. My mathematical input boundary is this packet alone plus those procedural rules and fixed logic/calculation allowance; I did not use source proofs or other task material. I make no claim of runtime isolation or external carrier attestation. The packet does not suffice for its stated conclusion. First unsupported implication in argument order: S002 asserts that the summand functions are measurable, hence AEMeasurable, because J_i∩[0,1] is Borel and the coefficient is constant. No permitted calculation or direct input proves measurability of the indicator/constant-times-indicator function. M002 requires AEMeasurability; listing that assertion in an application check is not a proof. This blocks the integral interchange and the subsequent slicing lower bound. Other local declaration inconsistencies are also noted in the closure checks.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The cited proposition IDs in R001 are present among the packet inputs. H001 and H002 have the stated roles; M001–M005 and M008–M014 are available conditional premises. This is not source-fidelity verification.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First unsupported implication: S002 claims each f(i,·)=ρ_i^s·1_{J_i∩[0,1]} is measurable (and thus AEMeasurable) from Borelness of J_i∩[0,1] and constancy of the coefficient. The packet supplies no applicable result or local proof of that measurability fact. M002 cannot therefore be applied as claimed. This blocks the integral/series interchange used to derive the covering-cost comparison and lower dimension bound. The separate assertion in S001 that isometries preserve the M008 formula is also not derived, though not the first gap.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inputs/1/source_contract\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The M002 application depends on an unproved measurability/AEMeasurability result, which is neither a direct input nor a locally established fact. In addition, the prose invokes several nontrivial-looking analytic/set-measure facts (for example, measurable indicators and restriction-measure identities); those uses cannot be supplied merely by the author's calculation policy or application notes.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The final prose claims dim_H(F)=dim_H(E)+1, matching the packet output after identifying F with E×[0,1] and I=[0,1]. This match does not establish derivation.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The argument divides into D=0 and D>0 cases and purports to combine upper and lower bounds, but the S002 lower-bound branch is blocked by the unsupported M002 applicability step. Some quantified limiting phrases (arbitrary q>D and arbitrary 0<s<D) are stated, but their downstream conclusions cannot be accepted.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M002's required per-index AEMeasurability is not established by the cited fact that the underlying set is Borel: the needed indicator measurability and multiplication step are not proved or otherwise supplied in this packet. The remaining mappings are not certified here as a substitute for that failed application.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inputs/1/source_contract\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input statements and output statement are available in full in the packet and can be understood without producer proofs. The output is the dimension identity for the product with I=[0,1].\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/output/statement\",\"/logic/primitives\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"There are material inventory/declaration mismatches. The local A_i has type 'projection of V_i to ℝⁿ' but its declaration instead defines ν; S002 lists A_i as an object without defining it as that projection. The local c_s is declared to be Hausdorff content but its declaration chooses an interval J_i, a different object. These undermine object registration and witness accounting. Other declarations also mismatch referenced index notation (for example N_i uses d_i while the stated diameter is d_{j,i}).\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/9\",\"/inference/locals/12\",\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/17\",\"/inference/argument/1/objects\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The actual factual use of measurability/AEMeasurability in S002 has no direct-input or earlier-local-proof basis. Moreover, an author assertion that the fact holds is not a derivation. The identified gap prevents closure of the M002-dependent argument.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/1/uses\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Mathematical conditional judgment: given the externally checked packet/carrier boundary, this packet alone does not suffice, because the M002 application has the unsupported measurability implication identified above. I read only the frozen packet as mathematical task material and the relevant declared Yui rules. I do not certify execution isolation, carrier identity, hash binding, or transmitted-material readback; those are outside this mathematical judgment, and missing runtime logs do not make this conditional mathematical verdict unverified.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"finding\":\"Unsupported implication: Borelness of J_i∩[0,1] and constancy of ρ_i^s imply that the summand function is measurable/AEMeasurable. No direct input or local proof establishes this prerequisite of M002. Consequently the integral interchange and ensuing lower-bound argument are not justified.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/locals/9\",\"finding\":\"A_i is typed as a projection of V_i to ℝⁿ, but its declaration defines ν rather than A_i.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/locals/12\",\"finding\":\"c_s is typed as Hausdorff content, but its declaration chooses J_i; this does not declare or witness c_s as typed.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/locals/17\",\"finding\":\"N_i is defined using d_i although the diameter variable declared in the packet is d_{j,i}; the notation/binding is inconsistent.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":